  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C1.S2 — Expectation value of a Pauli observable</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C1.S2 — Born rule and expectation values</p></div><p>Let \(|\psi\rangle=\cos(\theta/2)|0\rangle+\sin(\theta/2)|1\rangle\) with \(\theta\in[0,\pi]\).</p><p>(a) Give \(\langle\psi|Z|\psi\rangle\) as a simplified function of \(\theta\) (use <code>theta</code> for \(\theta\)).</p><p>\(\langle Z\rangle=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>(b) Give \(\langle\psi|X|\psi\rangle\) as a simplified function of \(\theta\).</p><p>\(\langle X\rangle=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Write \(|\psi\rangle=(\cos(\theta/2),\sin(\theta/2))^{T}\).</p><p>\(Z|\psi\rangle=(\cos(\theta/2),-\sin(\theta/2))^{T}\), so \(\langle Z\rangle=\cos^{2}(\theta/2)-\sin^{2}(\theta/2)=\cos\theta\).</p><p>\(X|\psi\rangle=(\sin(\theta/2),\cos(\theta/2))^{T}\), so \(\langle X\rangle=2\sin(\theta/2)\cos(\theta/2)=\sin\theta\).</p><p>These are precisely the \(z\)- and \(x\)-coordinates of the Bloch vector of \(|\psi\rangle\) (Chapter 2), confirming \(\langle X\rangle^2+\langle Y\rangle^2+\langle Z\rangle^2=1\) for a pure state.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
